      "text": "Let f be a function with a continuous derivative for all real x, where \\( f(2) = -1 \\), \\( f'(2) = 4 \\) and \\( f(4) = -2 \\), \\( f'(4) = 6 \\). Find \\( \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{f(2x) + 2}{x^{3} - 8} \\), showing the work that justifies the method.",
